Done. Zig 0.16 project at `artifacts/scd40/prompt0c`, all 16 tests pass.

**`src/main.zig`** — data conversion + reference functions with unit tests:
- CRC-8 (`0x31`, init `0xff`, no reflection/xor) — 23 datasheet vectors incl. `crc8Word(0xbeef)==0x92`
- CO₂ (identity), temp (`−45+175·w/65535`) and RH (`100·w/65535`) decode/encode
- temperature offset, sensor altitude, ambient pressure (`×100`), FRC (signed `w−0x8000`, `0xffff`=failed), ASC enable/target/periods
- serial number (48-bit, 3 words), data-ready (bits 10:0), sensor-variant (bits 15:12)
- encode out-of-range policies: saturate everywhere except `serialToRaw` → `error.OutOfRange`
- fuzz test verifying temp encode/decode round-trips within one count

**`conversions_manifest.md`** — the single source of truth: bit layout (full 16-bit word, big-endian), rounding = nearest + saturate, and per-function worked examples/policies.

Caught a real bug via the tests: my 48-bit sentinel literal `0x0000_ffff_ffff` was actually only 32 bits — fixed to `0xffff_ffff_ffff`. Also documented that datasheet example counts (e.g. 25 °C → `0x6667`) aren't exactly nearest-representable, so encoders may differ by ±1 count.
